{"format_version":1,"provider_address":"registry.terraform.io/ubiquiti-community/unifi","baseline_sha256":"1f5aff6f889192dd671e1dfd30fd0cf0e6c1b1e0addfe8664d7f17b516d77946","entries":[{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_account","baseline_schema_sha256":"f307755f376aedfc033ed23f79a1f26659d8deaebe0d3052cf30fa9a54241f7c","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_ap_group","baseline_schema_sha256":"9d15f4d629c579b63f559ac48107dd65222e03e1bdd821b0012070dad3ddd5fb","state":"generated_shadow","migration":"Schema compiles from the bootstrap and policy. id renames to the SDK's _id. site is provider-owned, not the SDK's site_id: the site name reaches the model as a function parameter and site_id is never read or written here, so matching on the name would have bound the wrong field. device_macs keeps its hwtypes.MACAddress element type, which neither referee can see, and its plan modifier moved to unifi/planmodifiers to be reachable from generated code. Admission waits on a campaign run.","implementation":"shadow"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_bgp","baseline_schema_sha256":"549a9fa273acebbc4cfd2d37d97f17ad2094c61fb1548ff404de67f2e2b4d606","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_client","baseline_schema_sha256":"4cdec2917133d131835a3e1d6f8ce94bf9f9e1d9bd11814c870fb7efc5ed804b","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_client_qos_rate","baseline_schema_sha256":"c9dd771f5228d615823efe89cee2970f6f403bcf370221541e2428344abfb926","state":"generated_shadow","migration":"Schema compiles from the bootstrap and policy. The surface fronts the SDK's ClientGroup, not a struct of its own name, so the bootstrap is derived from that type. id renames to _id; site is provider-owned rather than site_id, which this resource never reads or writes. Both rate defaults are int64default.StaticInt64(-1), transcribed by hand because the behaviour deriver stops at the unary minus rather than guessing. Admission waits on a campaign run.","implementation":"shadow"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_device","baseline_schema_sha256":"07a38835abeb0265967d8b196bb6d4943ea2323eeee1ae736cf8e885cf87daf0","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_dns_record","baseline_schema_sha256":"1bdb6740d88d68bf232d79874c34d0e3811d382f55948352add15c2a28e5e93c","state":"admitted","receipt_sha256":"dd3b22d7c5379c5c216c50439b09d6ff5e66c3be908076468f183ce5998dab19","implementation":"candidate"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_dynamic_dns","baseline_schema_sha256":"1ec15f3af56071fcbaccde8f0be3d9b60581eeeca38c33fe43e7ef31fce3a415","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_firewall_group","baseline_schema_sha256":"aee169dde322501484088563cfd6d96d8bf2ffcb0792765b033c5dc86c60b0a4","state":"generated_shadow","migration":"Schema compiles from the bootstrap and policy. Three renames read from the resource conversion code: id from _id, type from group_type, members from group_members. site is provider-owned rather than the SDK's site_id — firewallGroupToModel sets it from a parameter, and the update path's SiteID assignment writes the site name into that field rather than reading it. Descriptions are grafted back to plain, the second surface to need that. Admission waits on a campaign run.","implementation":"shadow"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_firewall_policy","baseline_schema_sha256":"ca4bef6da8db5460bc9ba1a398a2cd171e57ab950e51d3d7f9872d441bf6372c","state":"generated_shadow","migration":"Schema compiles from the catalog and policy and matches the released schema attribute for attribute, including both nested shapes. Admission waits on a campaign run, which is the only thing that can say whether the generated resource behaves as the hand-written one did.","implementation":"shadow"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_firewall_rule","baseline_schema_sha256":"5d4979f832f1cb67311f9d97e4671f7c0b3e0f2415f4a568b36f234d36b0bccc","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_firewall_zone","baseline_schema_sha256":"54f08886f9f75252ac7b351c222d8c517cf06f7e7a9680c508445903a2cb8b25","state":"generated_shadow","migration":"Schema compiles from the catalog and policy. Nine of the twelve SDK fields are controller bookkeeping the released schema never exposed and the policy omits by name. Admission waits on a campaign run.","implementation":"shadow"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_network","baseline_schema_sha256":"c37c9acf7f82ad07fce442a7b9aad5ba8d848a9dab4d4b7c915d499f64895fa5","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_port_forward","baseline_schema_sha256":"dec99a303604aa0a4d86ed8c6082ab616d404b6627f5996ca4b4d9fd479f71b6","state":"shadow_only","implementation":"shadow"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_port_profile","baseline_schema_sha256":"daf3a336e1308ca98e656cd9de83bccc0348570d983685d1f1095c5835e26b14","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_power_supervisor","baseline_schema_sha256":"00a4c7cb947db3e5ddb2a9f293d7021de46630b4fd0464ac9ef1dbd5c6ec78d1","state":"generated_shadow","migration":"Schema compiles from the catalog and policy, spreading the SDK Settings struct into the three duration attributes the released schema presents at the top level. Admission waits on a campaign run.","implementation":"shadow"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_radius_profile","baseline_schema_sha256":"fb32eaef59a7ac3e06cc5a311c3bd7f8b1aeab1108ccc0f54ad10faf36cdf02c","state":"policy_complete","implementation":"legacy"},{"kind":"managed_resource","name":"unifi_radius_user","baseline_schema_sha256":"8d4312510f9c7386cf0ecef658ddae43e9ecb0682df1493298e5b4245976797e","state":"policy_complete","implementatio